Each of those plugins carries the licence's text with its packs
(tools/fonts/NotoNaskhArabic-OFL.txt, NotoSerifHebrew-OFL.txt,
NotoSerifBengali-OFL.txt, NotoSerifDevanagari-OFL.txt,
NotoSerifEthiopic-OFL.txt, NotoSerifThai-OFL.txt, NotoSansThai-OFL.txt,
NotoSerifKhmer-OFL.txt, NotoSerifLao-OFL.txt, NotoSerifTibetan-OFL.txt,
NotoSerifGeorgian-OFL.txt, NotoSerifArmenian-OFL.txt, NotoSerifGujarati-OFL.txt,
NotoSerifGurmukhi-OFL.txt, NotoSerifOriya-OFL.txt, NotoSerifTamil-OFL.txt,
NotoSerifTelugu-OFL.txt, NotoSerifKannada-OFL.txt, NotoSerifMalayalam-OFL.txt,
NotoSerifSinhala-OFL.txt, NotoSerifMyanmar-OFL.txt, NotoSerif-OFL.txt,
NotoSans-OFL.txt, the text
given for Literata; NanumMyeongjo-OFL.txt, the same licence under its
own copyright and Reserved Font Names).

The words of the Khmer, Lao and Burmese letters plugins
(tools/khmer-words.txt, tools/lao-words.txt, tools/myanmar-words.txt,
which their packs carry for breaking lines) are taken from ICU's word
lists (khmerdict.txt, laodict.txt, burmesedict.txt), Copyright (C) 2016 and
later Unicode, Inc. and others, licensed under the Unicode License V3; the
Lao list also Copyright (C) 2013 Brian Eugene Wilson, Robert Martin
Campbell, under its BSD-style licence. Those plugins carry both texts
(tools/fonts/ICU-word-lists-LICENSE.txt).

Hyphenation patterns (plugins/hyphenation*/patterns: the data packs
of the store, English and twelve other languages; none is built in)
come from the hyph-utf8 project (https://github.com/hyphenation/tex-hyphen):

- German, reformed spelling, Copyright (c) 2013-2024 Stephan Hennig,
  Werner Lemberg, Günter Milde, Sander van Geloven, Georg Pfeiffer,
  Gisbert W. Selke, Tobias Wendorf, Keno Wehr, licensed under the MIT
  License.
- American English, Copyright (C) 1990, 2004, 2005 Gerard D.C. Kuiken,
  under an all-permissive license.

Their notices are in the patterns' README.md files.

The firmware of the Xteink readers also contains:

- Display initialisation sequences and waveform tables (for the Boox
  Picco also its touch, front light and battery tables) derived from the
  FreeInk SDK, Copyright (c) 2026 FreeInk, and the OpenX4 E-Paper
  Community SDK, Copyright (c) 2025 Open X4 E-Paper Contributors, both
  licensed under the MIT License (its text is below, with the crates').
- Battery gauge and board facts after Papyrix, Copyright (c) 2026 Pavel
  Liashkov, licensed under the MIT License.
- Mbed TLS (https://github.com/Mbed-TLS/mbedtls), Copyright The Mbed TLS
  Contributors, used under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (one of its
  two licences).
- The Wi-Fi, Bluetooth LE and radio libraries of ESP-IDF
  (https://github.com/espressif/esp-idf), Copyright Espressif Systems
  (Shanghai) Co., Ltd., provided as binaries for Espressif's chips and
  licensed as ESP-IDF states (Apache License, Version 2.0), and ESP-IDF's
  second-stage bootloader, licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.
- Mozilla's list of certificate authorities (webpki-roots), under the
  Community Data License Agreement Permissive 2.0, whose text is below.

Unicode data: the bidirectional and Arabic joining tables of
crates/paperpaw-text (src/bidi/tables.rs, src/arabic/tables.rs, made by
tools/unicode-tables.py), and its line-break class table
(src/linebreak/table_data.rs, made by tools/linebreak-table.py), are derived
from the Unicode Character Database,
and crates/paperpaw-text/tests/data/BidiCharacterTest-part.txt is a part of
its BidiCharacterTest.txt, Copyright (c) 1991-2026 Unicode, Inc., under the
Unicode License v3 (https://www.unicode.org/license.txt).

Patched copies of trouble-host, mbedtls-rs and jni-macros (patches/) keep their
licences; their changes are marked "Modified for PaperPaw".

crates/paperpaw-volume is PaperPaw's file-system driver. Its FAT code is
rust-fatfs 0.4 (https://github.com/rafalh/rust-fatfs), Copyright 2017 Rafał
Harabień, under the MIT licence (crates/paperpaw-volume/LICENSE.txt), cut down
and changed for PaperPaw; the changes are marked "Modified for PaperPaw".
Its exFAT code (crates/paperpaw-volume/src/exfat) is written for PaperPaw from
the exFAT code of hadris 3.0.0-rc (https://github.com/hxyulin/hadris),
Copyright (c) 2026 The Hadris Project Contributors, under the MIT licence
(crates/paperpaw-volume/LICENSE-hadris.txt).

The cats (the sleeping cat in plugins/sleep/pictures, the reading cats in
plugins/reading-goal/pictures, the README's pictures in docs/images/readme
and their dark versions) are PaperPaw artwork, generated with an AI
image model (Google Nano Banana) for the project, and licensed under the
Apache License, Version 2.0, as the rest of PaperPaw.
